From c4f98c2f4f6143929af172b3185d94ea1fc9c843 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Melhede <95473109+AMelhede@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:37:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rppg-web): add calibrationBlend: false so bpm shows the
 processor's resolved rate

When the processor's checks pass, bpm has been the camera calibration's
prediction from the spectral and autocorrelation rates. The model is never
trained against another sensor: untrained it is their plain mean, and it then
learns toward the resolved rate by a small step per read. When the two rates
disagree (the autocorrelation reads a clean 120 at 60), bpm is a blend
neither measured: 95.7 on one read, 115.5 after 14 reads at one a second.

With calibrationBlend: false (RppgProcessor's fourth argument, passed on by
createRppgSession), bpm is the resolved rate. The default, true, keeps the
previous behaviour exactly; calibrated_bpm still reports the prediction.
